  "id": "joint-friendly-strength",
  "name": "Joint-Friendly Strength",
  "description": "Three full-body workouts a week for 12 weeks, for older lifters, for anyone coming back after a long break, and for joints that do not like heavy barbells. Machines, dumbbells, the trap bar and the landmine keep the load easy to control; carries, single-leg work and band exercises train balance and the shoulders. Stop any exercise that hurts, and add weight slowly, only when every rep feels smooth. Check with a doctor first if you have a medical condition.",
